{title: Bread of the World in Mercy Broken}
{artist: Reginald Heber / John S. B. Hodges}
{genre: Hymn, Communion}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Response}
{key: D}
{key_original: Eb}
{tempo: 100}
{time: 3/4}
{c: Chords checked against the four-part harmony of the Cyber Hymnal score (The Hymnal of the Protestant Episcopal Church in the United States of America (New York: Church Pension Fund, 1940), # 196)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D]Bread of the world, in [A7]mercy [D7]broken,
[D7]Wine of the soul, in mer[A7]cy [D]shed!
[D]By whom the [G]words of [Em]life were spok[A]en,
[A]And [D]in [G]whose [Em]death [D]our sins__[A7]__ are [D]dead!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[D]Look on the heart by [A7]sorrow [D7]broken,
[D7]Look on the tears by sin[A7]ners [D]shed,
[D]And be Thy [G]feast to [Em]us the tok[A]en,
[A]That [D]by [G]Thy [Em]grace [D]our souls__[A7]__ are [D]fed!
{end_of_verse}
